{"name":"Hibernate","hex":"#aca69f","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"hibernate","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To spend the winter in a dormant or inactive state of minimal activity, low body temperature, slow breathing and heart rate, and low metabolic rate; to go through a winter sleep.","To live in seclusion."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hibernate"}],"entries":[{"title":"Hibernate (framework)","blocks":[{"text":"Hibernate ORM is an object–relational mapping tool for the Java programming language. It provides a framework for mapping an object-oriented domain model to a relational database. Hibernate handles object–relational impedance mismatch problems by replacing direct, persistent database accesses with high-level object handling functions."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hibernate_(framework)","wikidata":"Q747866"},{"title":"Hibernation","blocks":[{"text":"Hibernation is a state of minimal activity and metabolic reduction entered by some animal species. Hibernation is a seasonal heterothermy characterized by low body-temperature, slow breathing and heart-rate, and low metabolic rate. It is most commonly used to pass through winter months – called overwintering."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/35/Eptesicus_nilssonii_hibernating.JPG/330px-Eptesicus_nilssonii_hibernating.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hibernation","wikidata":"Q159408"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e1/Bat_in_mine_JAPAN.jpg/500px-Bat_in_mine_JAPAN.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e1/Bat_in_mine_JAPAN.jpg/1280px-Bat_in_mine_JAPAN.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e1/Bat_in_mine_JAPAN.jpg/500px-Bat_in_mine_JAPAN.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Bats hibernating in a silver mine","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABat_in_mine_JAPAN.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4d/Marmota_monax_UL_07.jpg/500px-Marmota_monax_UL_07.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4d/Marmota_monax_UL_07.jpg/1280px-Marmota_monax_UL_07.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4d/Marmota_monax_UL_07.jpg/500px-Marmota_monax_UL_07.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Groundhog gathering nesting material for its warm burrow in preparation for hibernation","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMarmota_monax_UL_07.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/8/85/Bear_hibernating.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/8/85/Bear_hibernating.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"Black bear mother and cubs \"denning\"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABear_hibernating.jpg"}],"sounds":{"hibernate":[{"type":"audio/wav","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/2/22/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-hibernate.wav?utm_source=en.wiktionary.org&utm_campaign=rest&utm_content=original"},{"type":"audio/mpeg","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/2/22/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-hibernate.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-hibernate.wav.mp3"},{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/2/22/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-hibernate.wav/LL-Q1860_%28eng%29-Vealhurl-hibernate.wav.ogg"}]}